{"map":{"title":"Geologic Map of Mars","citation":"Tanaka, K.L., Skinner, J.A., Jr., Dohm, J.M., Irwin, R.P., III, Kolb, E.J., Fortezzo, C.M., Platz, T., Michael, G.G., and Hare, T.M., 2014, Geologic map of Mars: U.S. Geological Survey Scientific Investigations Map 3292, scale 1:20,000,000.","sim":"SIM 3292","scale":"1:20,000,000","scale_denominator":20000000,"scale_note":"At 1:20,000,000 one millimetre is 20 km and boundaries are positioned to a few kilometres at best; the twin is 2.4 x 3.0 km, so what it shows is which unit the map assigns to this spot, not a boundary location.","no_larger_scale":"No larger-scale USGS geologic map of Gale crater exists in the USGS publications warehouse or the Planetary Geologic Mapping hub (Mars SIMs at 1:1M or larger cover Jezero, Shalbatana, Athabasca, Nepenthes, Ladon, Candor, Olympus Mons).","url":"https://pubs.usgs.gov/sim/3292/","hub":"https://astrogeology-usgs.hub.arcgis.com/pages/interactive-maps-mars","service":"https://services.arcgis.com/v01gqwM5QqNysAAi/arcgis/rest/services/Tanaka_et_al_2014_Mars_Global_Map_Features/FeatureServer/3","credit":"USGS Astrogeology Science Center / USGS-NASA Planetary Geologic Mapping Program","fetched_utc":"2026-11-13T17:29:45Z"},"w":585,"h":732,"units":["AHi","Htu"],"data":"","encoding":"zlib deflate, uint8 unit index per cell, row-major from the north-west cell","legend":[{"code":"AHi","name":"Amazonian and Hesperian impact unit","group":"Impact Unit","age":"Hesperian to Amazonian (mapped as spanning both epochs)","color":[255,255,0],"primary":"Craters with rims and surrounding blankets; some include single to multi-lobed blanket forms, dense secondary crater chains, and (or) central peak or pit. Blanket thicknesses of meters to a few hundred meters.","additional":"Global occurrence. Superposes Noachian units; other unit superposition relations diverse. High kilometer-scale surface roughness; crater floors may be smooth to rough.","interpretation":"Upturned, ejected, and brecciated target rocks and sediments, with local areas of impact melt. Post-impact mass-wasting and fluvial-lacustrine and eolian infill of craters common.","cells":0,"pct":0.0},{"code":"Htu","name":"Hesperian transition undivided unit","group":"Transition Units","age":"Hesperian","color":[204,204,204],"primary":"Irregular plateaus hundreds of kilometers across. Layered. Hundreds of meters to kilometers thick.","additional":"In southern Elysium Planitia along highland/lowland boundary and within and east of Valles Marineris. Superposes units Nhu, Nve, mNh, and eNh; gradational with units eHt, Hve, and HNt (Hesperian part); overlain by units lHt, Ht, Hto, AHtu, Aa, and lAv. Includes hydrated sulfate spectral signatures; fluted slopes in places. Linear ridges, anabranching sinuous ridges, and wrinkle ridges common.","interpretation":"Fine-grained eolian sediments and (or) pyroclastic air-fall deposits. Modified by fluvial dissection and eolian erosion. Linear ridges and grooves form yardangs. Tectonically contracted. Channels mostly inverted. Altered by acidic weathering in places.","cells":428220,"pct":100.0}],"context":{"window":[137.0,137.8,-5.2,-4.4],"polygons":[{"code":"AHi","rings":[[[138.0271,-2.3214],[138.0398,-2.3226],[138.0742,-2.3281],[138.0827,-2.3296],[138.0912,-2.3314],[138.1036,-2.335],[138.1196,-2.3416],[138.1548,-2.3583],[138.1652,-2.3646],[138.1681,-2.3669],[138.1705,-2.3694],[138.1722,-2.3723],[138.1731,-2.3755],[138.1734,-2.379],[138.1732,-2.3827],[138.1727,-2.3866],[138.1687,-2.4028],[138.1662,-2.4112],[138.1624,-2.4237],[138.1584,-2.4362],[138.1557,-2.4445],[138.151,-2.4567],[138.1282,-2.504],[138.1235,-2.515],[138.1224,-2.5184],[138.1217,-2.5215],[138.1216,-2.5241],[138.1224,-2.5263],[138.1241,-2.5278],[138.1267,-2.5288],[138.1299,-2.5293],[138.1336,-2.5296],[138.1375,-2.5297],[138.146,-2.5294],[138.1818,-2.5269],[138.1994,-2.5245],[138.2037,-2.5235],[138.2077,-2.5223],[138.2118,-2.5209],[138.2157,-2.5193],[138.2586,-2.4987],[138.2703,-2.4939],[138.2821,-2.49